    imaging: 'CT Abdomen: 4.5 cm heterogeneous mass in right adrenal gland. MRI: T2-hyperintense right adrenal mass with >10 HU on non-contrast.',
    diagnosis: 'Pheochromocytoma (Right Adrenal Gland)',
    ddx: ['Pheochromocytoma', 'Essential Hypertension', 'Panic Disorder', 'Thyrotoxicosis', 'Carcinoid Syndrome', 'Sympathomimetic Drug Use', 'Paroxysmal Supraventricular Tachycardia'],
    goals: 'Prevent hypertensive crises, prepare for surgical resection, avoid intraoperative catecholamine storm.',
    pharm: '1. PHENTOLAMINE (alpha-blockade FIRST): Phenoxybenzamine 10 mg PO BID, titrate by 10 mg every 2–3 days until BP controlled (target 30–60 mg daily). Or doxazosin 2–8 mg daily. 2. AFTER alpha-blockade established: Add propranolol 20–40 mg TID. 3. For hypertensive crisis: IV phentolamine 5–10 mg bolus. 4. Metyrosine 250 mg QID (inhibits tyrosine hydroxylase) as adjunct.',
