    dtps: '1. MUST achieve alpha-blockade FIRST before giving beta-blockers — beta-blockade alone causes unopposed alpha-mediated vasoconstriction leading to hypertensive crisis. 2. Phenoxybenzamine is non-competitive, long-acting alpha-blocker preferred for preoperative preparation.',
    monitoring: 'BP monitoring 4 times daily in supine and standing positions. Preoperative: plasma metanephrines, ECG, echocardiogram. Intraoperative: invasive arterial monitoring.',
    counselling: 'Most pheochromocytomas are benign but require surgical removal. Carry a medical alert card. Avoid triggers: alcohol, tyramine-rich foods, physical exertion during crises. Inform all healthcare providers.',
